    "claims": [
      {
        "text": "It is rank three, can move ten thousand miles, and is the number one mount under rank five, but its great weakness is that it can fly only once: the moment it lands is the moment of its death. Fang Yuan takes out another footless bird Gu obtained as a King Xin Inheritance reward, feeds refinement materials and primeval stones into it, and produces rank four Bone Wings Gu.",
        "chapters": [
          358
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "rank-and-a-later-copy",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "inh_king_xin_inheritance"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "That feed is refinement stock for Bone Wings Gu, not a feeding rule for keeping a living mount. That King Xin copy is separate from the Bai Gu mountain bird listed as destroyed in chapter 228.",
        "chapters": [
          228
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "citation_unchecked",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "rank-and-a-later-copy",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "gu_bone_wings_gu",
          "char_king_xin"
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
  "appearance": {
    "claims": [
      {
        "text": "Unused, it is a quail-egg-sized bone ball covered with black and white stripes, like a zebra.",
        "chapters": [
          225
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "appearance",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      },
      {
        "text": "A second copy has the same inactive look: a ball of bone the size of a quail egg, with alternating black and white stripes like a zebra.",
        "chapters": [
          358
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "appearance",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      },
      {
        "text": "When summoned it is a white bone bird with no flesh or blood. It has an eagle’s head, a crane’s body, a swallow’s tail, two pairs of wings, and no legs. The wings are thin bone pieces.",
        "chapters": [
          227
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "citation_unchecked",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "appearance",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      },
      {
        "text": "When summoned underfoot it is a white bone bird with no flesh or blood: eagle head, crane body, swallow tail, four wings, and no legs.",
        "chapters": [
          227
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "citation_unchecked",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "form",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      },
      {
        "text": "In inactive form it is the striped bone ball described above.",
        "chapters": [
          225
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "form",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      }
    ],
    "visual_confidence": "text_described"
  },
  "abilities": {
    "activation_raw": null,
    "claims": [
      {
        "text": "It is a movement type Gu that can be used only once, with a large body able to fly thousands of miles.",
        "chapters": [
          225
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "effect",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "sys_movement_gu"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Bai clan observers call it able to fly ten thousand miles in a day, and say that under rank five it is the number one flying steed, with few Gu able to match its speed. During the climb from the cliff, Fang Yuan’s primeval essence drops rapidly while Heavenly Essence Treasure Lotus keeps feeding his sea.",
        "chapters": [
          227
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "citation_unchecked",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "effect",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "gu_heavenly_essence_treasure_lotus"
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
